Relevant columns and why they matter  
bigquery-public-data.new_york.citibike_trips  
• starttime / stoptime : derive calendar day of a trip (UTC in this table).  
• tripduration, bikeid, … : any column could be used to count trips; the safest is simply COUNT(*) for each day.  

bigquery-public-data.ghcn_d.ghcnd_stations  
• id : join‐key to daily measurements.  
• latitude / longitude : find the closest station to NYC (40.7128 N, –74.0060 E).  

bigquery-public-data.ghcn_d.ghcnd_2016                      (and only this daily fact table is needed)  
• id : join‐key to station meta table.  
• date : calendar day of the observation.  
• element : choose 'PRCP' (daily precipitation total).  
• value : precipitation in tenths of millimetres; divide by 10.  
• qflag : quality flag – must be NULL to ensure an unflagged, valid value.  

Typical filter / join conditions  
• element = 'PRCP' and qflag IS NULL                                    -- keep only good precip values  
• DATE(starttime) BETWEEN '2016-01-01' AND '2016-12-31'                  -- restrict CitiBike trips  
• ST_DISTANCE(ST_GEOGPOINT(longitude, latitude),  
              ST_GEOGPOINT(-74.0060, 40.7128)) < 50 000                  --  ≤50 km to NYC  

Below are ten exploratory‑to‑final SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows except the last) that gradually build the complete solution.

```sql
-- 1) Peek at CitiBike trips in 2016
SELECT *
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.new_york.citibike_trips`
WHERE  DATE(starttime) BETWEEN '2016-01-01' AND '2016-12-31'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Count CitiBike trips for a handful of January‑2016 days
SELECT DATE(starttime)          AS trip_day,
       COUNT(*)                 AS trips
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.new_york.citibike_trips`
WHERE  DATE(starttime) BETWEEN '2016-01-01' AND '2016-01-15'
GROUP  BY trip_day
ORDER  BY trip_day
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Find GHCN stations within 50 km of Times Sq (‑74.0060, 40.7128)
SELECT id,
       name,
       latitude,
       longitude,
       ST_DISTANCE(ST_GEOGPOINT(longitude, latitude),
                   ST_GEOGPOINT(-74.0060, 40.7128)) AS distance_m
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ghcn_d.ghcnd_stations`
WHERE  ST_DISTANCE(ST_GEOGPOINT(longitude, latitude),
                   ST_GEOGPOINT(-74.0060, 40.7128)) < 50000
ORDER  BY distance_m
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Inspect what climate elements are available for the nearest station
SELECT DISTINCT element
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ghcn_d.ghcnd_2016`
WHERE  id = 'USW00094728'          -- (example JFK airport station)
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Look at raw daily precipitation for that station (first 20 rows)
SELECT date,
       value                      AS prcp_tenths_mm,
       value/10.0                 AS prcp_mm
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ghcn_d.ghcnd_2016`
WHERE  id      = 'USW00094728'
  AND  element = 'PRCP'
  AND  qflag IS NULL
ORDER  BY date
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Aggregate daily precipitation for 2016 at chosen station
SELECT date,
       SUM(value)/10.0 AS prcp_mm
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ghcn_d.ghcnd_2016`
WHERE  id      = 'USW00094728'
  AND  element = 'PRCP'
  AND  qflag IS NULL
  AND  date BETWEEN '2016-01-01' AND '2016-12-31'
GROUP  BY date
ORDER  BY date
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Flag each 2016 day as Rainy (>5 mm) or Not‑rainy
WITH pr AS (
  SELECT date,
         SUM(value)/10.0 AS prcp_mm
  FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ghcn_d.ghcnd_2016`
  WHERE  id      = 'USW00094728'
    AND  element = 'PRCP'
    AND  qflag IS NULL
    AND  date BETWEEN '2016-01-01' AND '2016-12-31'
  GROUP  BY date )
SELECT date,
       prcp_mm,
       CASE WHEN prcp_mm > 5 THEN 'rainy' ELSE 'non_rainy' END AS rain_flag
FROM   pr
ORDER  BY date
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Daily CitiBike trip counts joined to rain flag (sample)
WITH trips AS (
  SELECT DATE(starttime) AS trip_day,
         COUNT(*)        AS trips
  FROM   `bigquery-public-data.new_york.citibike_trips`
  WHERE  DATE(starttime) BETWEEN '2016-01-01' AND '2016-12-31'
  GROUP  BY trip_day),
pr AS (
  SELECT date,
         SUM(value)/10.0 AS prcp_mm
  FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ghcn_d.ghcnd_2016`
  WHERE  id      = 'USW00094728'
    AND  element = 'PRCP'
    AND  qflag IS NULL
    AND  date BETWEEN '2016-01-01' AND '2016-12-31'
  GROUP  BY date)
SELECT t.trip_day,
       t.trips,
       IFNULL(pr.prcp_mm,0)                              AS prcp_mm,
       CASE WHEN IFNULL(pr.prcp_mm,0) > 5 THEN 'rainy'
            ELSE 'non_rainy' END                         AS rain_flag
FROM   trips t
LEFT  JOIN pr
       ON t.trip_day = pr.date
ORDER  BY t.trip_day
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Average daily trips on rainy vs non‑rainy days (quick result preview)
WITH trips AS (
  SELECT DATE(starttime) AS trip_day,
         COUNT(*)        AS trips
  FROM   `bigquery-public-data.new_york.citibike_trips`
  WHERE  DATE(starttime) BETWEEN '2016-01-01' AND '2016-12-31'
  GROUP  BY trip_day),
pr AS (
  SELECT date,
         SUM(value)/10.0 AS prcp_mm
  FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ghcn_d.ghcnd_2016`
  WHERE  id      = 'USW00094728'
    AND  element = 'PRCP'
    AND  qflag IS NULL
    AND  date BETWEEN '2016-01-01' AND '2016-12-31'
  GROUP  BY date),
joined AS (
  SELECT t.trip_day,
         t.trips,
         IFNULL(pr.prcp_mm,0) AS prcp_mm
  FROM   trips t
  LEFT  JOIN pr
         ON t.trip_day = pr.date )
SELECT CASE WHEN prcp_mm > 5 THEN 'rainy' ELSE 'non_rainy' END AS rain_flag,
       AVG(trips)                                             AS avg_daily_trips
FROM   joined
GROUP  BY rain_flag
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Final full‑year answer: average daily CitiBike trips, rainy vs non‑rainy
WITH
-- daily CitiBike trips in 2016
daily_trips AS (
  SELECT DATE(starttime) AS trip_day,
         COUNT(*)        AS trips
  FROM   `bigquery-public-data.new_york.citibike_trips`
  WHERE  DATE(starttime) BETWEEN '2016-01-01' AND '2016-12-31'
  GROUP  BY trip_day ),
-- choose the single closest GHCN station ≤50 km (ordered by distance)
closest_station AS (
  SELECT id
  FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ghcn_d.ghcnd_stations`
  WHERE  ST_DISTANCE(ST_GEOGPOINT(longitude, latitude),
                     ST_GEOGPOINT(-74.0060, 40.7128)) < 50000
  ORDER  BY ST_DISTANCE(ST_GEOGPOINT(longitude, latitude),
                        ST_GEOGPOINT(-74.0060, 40.7128))
  LIMIT 1 ),
-- daily precipitation (mm) for that station in 2016
daily_prcp AS (
  SELECT date,
         SUM(value)/10.0 AS prcp_mm
  FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ghcn_d.ghcnd_2016`  g
  JOIN   closest_station c
    ON   g.id = c.id
  WHERE  element = 'PRCP'
    AND  qflag  IS NULL
    AND  date BETWEEN '2016-01-01' AND '2016-12-31'
  GROUP  BY date ),
-- combine bike counts with precipitation, defaulting precip to 0
daily_combined AS (
  SELECT d.trip_day,
         d.trips,
         IFNULL(p.prcp_mm,0) AS prcp_mm
  FROM   daily_trips d
  LEFT  JOIN daily_prcp p
         ON d.trip_day = p.date )
-- final aggregation
SELECT CASE WHEN prcp_mm > 5 THEN 'rainy'
            ELSE 'non_rainy' END      AS rain_flag,
       AVG(trips)                     AS average_daily_trips
FROM   daily_combined
GROUP  BY rain_flag
ORDER  BY rain_flag;
```

The last query will return two rows:  
• rain_flag = 'rainy'     — average number of CitiBike trips per rainy day in 2016.  
• rain_flag = 'non_rainy' — average number of trips per non‑rainy day in 2016.  
